 "note": "Quick, Draw! bus 6409748716978176, facing left. Stroke 0 is the body: a stepped front with the windshield at the left, the long roof, the back end and the bottom edge. Stroke 1 is the row of windows drawn as one zigzag line. Stroke 2 is the front wheel and stroke 3 the rear wheel, each a lumpy loop. The rig places the whole drawing as one rigid body by two points at mid height on its front and back ends, keyed on the front edge of the bus and its length, so it moves and grows as the bus comes toward the camera. The wheels are not spun: turning a lumpy oval about its centre makes it tumble instead of roll.",
